ryan giggs arrived for the second day of  his trial to hear the woman he's accused  of assaulting describe in graphic detail  the events of that night in november  2020. kate gravel said she'd already  decided to end her relationship with the  former footballer for good when another  argument began during a night out in  manchester  when she returned to the home they  shared to pack up her belongings he  followed and a struggle began he pushed  her backwards she told the jury and  pinned her to the floor he pushed her  head into the ground she thought he'd  broken her elbow  that's when he came up to my face and  head butted me she said he came at me  from nowhere grabbed me by the shoulders  and head butted me in the face i said i  can't believe you've just done that i  was in shock and fell backwards my lip  instantly swelled so i put my hands over  my mouth and i was really worried  because i could taste the blood and  thought he'd split my lip open  all the other times he'd hurt me this  was different he really wanted to hurt  me he looked me straight in the eyes and  headbutted me when she wanted to call  the police he said you need to think  about this kate it will ruin me and ruin  you he was saying think about my job  think about my career think about my  kids and i said then you shouldn't have  done it earlier the court had been  played kate grevel's police interview  from the time in which she described a  number of incidents over the years in  one she said mr giggs had grabbed her  wrists and dragged her naked out of a  hotel room in another he kicked her so  hard in the back she flew off a bed he  then threw a bag containing a laptop at  her head leaving her she said crying her  eyes out on the floor the jury was shown  a number of images of injuries alleged  to have been caused by mr giggs  she said at the start of their  relationship she thought ryan giggs was  her soul mate it was the best thing ever  she said a love story like in the movies  but she was already seeing what she  called red flags abusive messages and  threats to reveal things about their  relationship  ryan giggs left court having heard his  former girlfriend say she felt isolated  and helpless in their relationship and  that that's why she went back to him he  denies the charges against him her  evidence continues greg milam sky news  manchester
 

